:: > FOR DEVS {"position":"575,375","size":"100,100"}
''Brief style guide:''
* Anything written in (color:yellow)[yellow] is an optional detail. This will add a click to the click timer, but give the player more flavor text about the given concept. This will not take the player to a new page. 
* (color:blue)[Blue] links take the player to a new page. They also add a click to the click timer, unless they are labelled "Back." and chain back into hub2.
* Names of nodes can be changed to better fit the narrative context, but ensure that you use the "Rename" function at the top of the window--otherwise, a new node will be created without any of the native text or code. 

''Brief overview of the code:''
* hub2 operates on a click-based "timer", which shows the passage of time via the amount of clicks the player has made over the course of the game. In order to ensure this stays consistent throughout, any (color:blue)[blue] or (color:yellow)[yellow] links need to add +1 to the '$ clicks' variable. This will ensure the display changes on the hub page, and the failstate triggers properly. 
* Interactable 3 and 5 both have a chance to spawn the code1 item, and Interactable 6 and 8 have a chance to spawn the code2 item. If both attempts trigger the fail dialogue, these areas can be 're-searched' until the success dialogue triggers. Once a code item is found, that code item //shouldn't// be findable again--but if you find, during testing, that this isn't the case... whoops.
* Interactable 4 has a very slim chance to give you the full code. I thought it would be funny. It can be taken out very easily. 
* The code entry page will only proceed to the two ending branches if the correct code is entered; you do not need to have found all code items to do this, but every attempt takes a click. Currently, I have it configured so that you lock yourself into the gun ending as soon as you take the gun. 
* You must have unlocked the safe (and taken the herbs) to get the cure option to appear in the lab.


